description: Next.js App Router patterns used in this project
globs: app/**/*
---

## App Router
- Pages live under `app/<segment>/page.tsx` with optional `loading.tsx`.
- Nested dynamic routes use `[id]/page.tsx`.
- Shared layout is defined in `app/layout.tsx`.

## Current Routes
- Root: `app/page.tsx`
- Auth: `app/auth/login/page.tsx`, `app/auth/sign-up/page.tsx`, `app/auth/update-password/page.tsx`, and others under `auth/*`.
- Search: `app/search/page.tsx`, dynamic: `app/search/[id]/page.tsx`, loading UI in `app/search/loading.tsx`.
- Share: `app/share/[id]/page.tsx`, loading UI in `app/share/loading.tsx`.

## API Routes
- Implemented under `app/api/*` using route handlers (single-file `route.ts` or function exports per current structure).
- Subtrees include: `advanced-search`, `chat`, `chats`, `config`, `ollama`.

## Conventions
- Co-locate components used only by a route next to it when practical.
- Prefer server components by default; add `'use client'` when interactivity is needed.

